# Rules

## Headings

| Name | ID | Fix | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `first-line-heading` | MD041 | no | Comments aside, the file starts with a top-level heading or front matter title. |
| `heading-blank-lines` | MD022 | yes | Headings have a blank or comment line above and below. |
| `heading-increment` | MD001 | no | Each heading is at most one level deeper than the heading or title before it. |
| `heading-start-left` | MD023 | yes | Headings start at the beginning of their line, list item or blockquote. |
| `heading-style` | MD003 | yes | Headings all use the first heading's style: \# Title, \# Title \#, or underlined. |
| `no-duplicate-heading` | MD024 | no | No two headings have exactly the same text. |
| `no-emphasis-as-heading` | MD036 | yes | Outside lists and blockquotes, a bold or italic line is not a stand-in heading. |
| `no-missing-space-atx` | MD018 | yes | A space follows the \# marks that open a heading at the start of a line. |
| `no-missing-space-closed-atx` | MD020 | yes | A closed heading at the start of a line has a space inside each run of \#. |
| `no-multiple-space-atx` | MD019 | yes | Only one space follows the \# marks that open a heading. |
| `no-multiple-space-closed-atx` | MD021 | yes | A closed heading has only one space inside each run of \#. |
| `no-trailing-punctuation` | MD026 | yes | Headings do not end with a period, comma, semicolon, colon or exclamation mark. |
| `required-headings` | MD043 | no | Headings follow the configured outline in order. No outline is set by default. |
| `single-h1` | MD025 | no | A document that starts with a title has no other top-level heading. |

## Lists

| Name | ID | Fix | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `blanks-around-lists` | MD032 | yes | Lists outside other lists have a blank or comment line above and below. |
| `list-indent` | MD005 | yes | Items in a list start at the same column. Ordered numbers may right-align. |
| `list-marker-space` | MD030 | yes | One space, or one tab, separates each list marker from the item's text. |
| `ol-prefix` | MD029 | yes | Ordered list items are numbered 1, 1, 1, or 1, 2, 3, or 0, 1, 2, and so on. |
| `ul-indent` | MD007 | yes | Outside ordered lists, bullets sit at the margin and indent 2 spaces per level. |
| `unordered-list-style` | MD004 | yes | Every bullet uses the same marker as the first bullet in the file. |

## Whitespace and layout

| Name | ID | Fix | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `hr-style` | MD035 | yes | Every horizontal rule is written the same way as the first one, such as ---. |
| `line-length` | MD013 | yes | Lines fit in 80 characters, with exemptions such as lone links and definitions. |
| `no-hard-tabs` | MD010 | yes | Lines contain no tab characters, including inside code. |
| `no-multiple-blank-lines` | MD012 | yes | Outside code, no two blank lines follow each other, except after front matter. |
| `no-trailing-spaces` | MD009 | yes | Outside code blocks, lines end in no spaces or tabs, or in exactly 2 of them. |
| `single-trailing-newline` | MD047 | yes | The file ends with a newline, or a last line of only whitespace, \> or comments. |

## Code

| Name | ID | Fix | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `blanks-around-fences` | MD031 | yes | Fenced code blocks have a blank or comment line above and below. |
| `code-block-style` | MD046 | no | Code blocks all use the first block's style, fenced or indented. |
| `code-fence-style` | MD048 | yes | Code fences all use the first fence's character, backtick or tilde. |
| `commands-show-output` | MD014 | yes | Code blocks that show only commands leave out the \$ prompt. |
| `fenced-code-language` | MD040 | yes | Fenced code blocks name their language after the opening fence. |
| `no-space-in-code` | MD038 | yes | Code span text has no spaces around it, except one each side or by a backtick. |

## Links and images

| Name | ID | Fix | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `descriptive-link-text` | MD059 | no | Link text describes its target instead of saying "click here" or "more". |
| `link-destination-style` | MDL001 | no | Relative links and local file: URLs are not mixed in one document. |
| `link-fragments` | MD051 | no | Links to a \#fragment point at a heading or anchor in the same file, or at \#top. |
| `link-image-reference-definitions` | MD053 | yes | Every reference definition is used and defined once, except \[//\] comments. |
| `link-image-style` | MD054 | no | Links and images use only the allowed styles. By default, all are allowed. |
| `no-alt-text` | MD045 | no | Markdown images have alt text, and HTML images have alt or aria-hidden="true". |
| `no-bare-urls` | MD034 | yes | Outside code and HTML, URLs and email addresses sit in angle brackets or links. |
| `no-empty-links` | MD042 | no | Inline links have a destination, and no link points at just \#. |
| `no-reversed-links` | MD011 | yes | Inline links put the text in brackets and the URL in parentheses: \[text\](url). |
| `no-space-in-links` | MD039 | yes | Link text has no spaces just inside its brackets. |
| `reference-links-images` | MD052 | no | Labels in \[text\]\[label\] and \[label\]\[\] references are defined, except x. |

## Tables

| Name | ID | Fix | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `blanks-around-tables` | MD058 | yes | Tables have a blank or comment line above and below. |
| `table-alignment` | MDL003 | yes | Each cell of a table's delimiter row has at least 3 dashes. |
| `table-column-count` | MD056 | no | Every table row has as many cells as the header row. |
| `table-column-style` | MD060 | no | Each table follows one style: aligned pipes, one space of padding, or none. |
| `table-pipe-style` | MD055 | no | Table rows use leading and trailing pipes the same way throughout. |

## Emphasis

| Name | ID | Fix | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `emphasis-style` | MD049 | yes | All italic text uses one marker, \*text\* or \_text\_, except \* inside a word. |
| `no-space-in-emphasis` | MD037 | yes | Emphasis markers touch the text they wrap, as in \*\*bold\*\*. |
| `strong-style` | MD050 | yes | All bold text uses one marker, \*\*text\*\* or \_\_text\_\_, except \*\* inside a word. |

## Blockquotes

| Name | ID | Fix | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `no-blanks-blockquote` | MD028 | no | No blank line sits between two blockquotes. |
| `no-multiple-space-blockquote` | MD027 | yes | Outside code and list item text, at most one space follows a blockquote's \>. |

